1
00:00:01,021 --> 00:00:05,611
Who opened that chart, and when? — Two clicks, not a two-week search.

2
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:12,839
Every action, with the user and the address behind it.

3
00:00:12,839 --> 00:00:20,052
Note the views. Opening a chart leaves a trace, not just changing it.

4
00:00:20,052 --> 00:00:27,565
Filter by action, user, module or date, and the list is the handful that matter.

5
00:00:27,565 --> 00:00:35,822
One entry: who, what, when, and from where.

6
00:00:35,822 --> 00:00:41,855
The trail says what happened. This says why it was allowed.

7
00:00:41,855 --> 00:00:48,917
Every role, every module, spelled out rather than assumed.

8
00:00:48,917 --> 00:00:52,860
And the record is not trapped here.

9
00:00:52,860 --> 00:01:00,313
FHIR R4 — a diagnosis is a Condition, a vital sign an Observation.

10
00:01:00,313 --> 00:01:06,119
Downloadable as standard JSON, readable by a system that has never heard of us.

11
00:01:07,049 --> 00:01:12,809
Answerable. Explainable. Portable. — The three things an auditor actually asks for.
